<title>TURKEY: Turkish Eregli Q1 net profits up 19 pct.</title>
<headline>Turkish Eregli Q1 net profits up 19 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-March 1997 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)   321.08 vs     270.17</p>
<p>    Net profit		  2,034.34 vs   1,711.78</p>
<p>    Net sales		  28,948.79 vs  11,251.85</p>
<p>    Operating profit	  8,190.64 vs   2,669.92</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	3,077.75 vs   1,528.47</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense     1,325.55 vs	39.55</p>
<p>    Interest paid	     6,421.81 vs   2,064.82</p>
<p>    Extraordinary expense   1,178.62 vs	85.55</p>
<p>    Total debts		99,960.59 vs  58,577.93</p>
<p>    Equity		     51,882.06 vs  29,961.09</p>
<p>    Capital		     6,336.00 vs   6,336.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkey's largely state-owned flat steel maker Eregli Demir ve Celik Fabrikalari T.A.S. is slated for partial sell off, with 51 66 percent of its capital held by the privatisation administration OIB.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 77 percent annual wholesale in March.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875.</p>
</text>
